**Read:** [Inorganic Chemical Technology — Nanda Kishore, NPTEL](../sources/Inorganic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_77Z8T5RFYFNNXZ7XKZFKPRKDKR), the entire sulfuric-acid manufacturing sequence; [Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals — Ammonia, Acids and Fertilisers, BREF LVIC-AAF](../sources/Ammonia-Acids-Fertilisers-BREF.lingua#r_45NWBJYAMXXSRV071A57EM02GB), the complete sulfuric-acid chapter with feed, heat recovery, absorption and residuals; [Chemical-industry process descriptions and emission factors — EPA AP-42](../sources/Chemical-Industry-Emission-Factors-EPA.lingua#r_16XA95GZSY1VD7GZNTSXWVNBC3), the whole sulfuric-acid process/factor and background sections.

Sulfuric-acid production connects sulfur-oxide generation, catalytic conversion, gas conditioning and absorption into the required acid state. S+O₂→SO₂ and 2SO₂+O₂⇌2SO₃ provide part of the chemical account. The relation SO₃+H₂O→H₂SO₄ is a stoichiometric statement, not a description of all practical absorption and mist behavior.

Gas composition, contaminants, catalyst condition, temperature profiles and heat recovery interact. Equilibrium and finite rates influence conversion; absorption and entrainment influence what reaches the product and residual gas. Different sulfur-bearing feeds can require different preparation and impurity handling even when the final acid specification is similar.

Define acid concentration, water/oleum basis and consequential contaminants. Trace the sulfur through product, returned material, mist, tail gas, wastewater and deposits. Energy recovered as steam is useful only on a compatible temperature, time and product boundary.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete public acid route and derive its sulfur/oxygen/water and thermal accounts independently. Compare two documented contact/absorption arrangements or feed sources at equal accepted acid output. Explain how actual catalyst, gas, absorption and monitoring evidence supports the comparison, including influential uncertainty and changed conditions.

